# Documentation

Every exported function, class, method, type, constant, and component has a short English JSDoc comment. Every field of a type or interface has one too, immediately above the field.

- Say what the value means: the result, the unit, and when it is empty.
- Do not retell the implementation. A comment that walks through the steps, names the formula, or repeats the code is noise.
- Do not mention the server, storage, a rejected write, a sent payload, or when a fetch happens.
- One or two sentences. Skip comments on re-exports and on private helpers.
- Re-export barrels stay uncommented. The declaration they point at carries the comment.

```typescript
// Bad: the comment repeats the steps
/** Filters rows, sorts by start time, and slices to 40. */
export function recentPerformances(rows: readonly MatchPerformance[]): readonly MatchPerformance[] {}

// Good: the comment states the result
/** Newest matches, optionally limited to one hero. */
export function recentPerformances(rows: readonly MatchPerformance[]): readonly MatchPerformance[] {}

// Bad: the comment names the server and the stored form
/** Country code as typed. The server stores the uppercase form. */

// Good
/** Country code. */
```
